# dbt Rules

## Adapter

Use `dbt-trino` only. All models target the `iceberg` catalog in Trino at `http://trino:8090`.

## Model Layer Rules

**Staging (`models/staging/`):**
- Source: `raw.*` Iceberg tables
- Clean types, handle nulls, deduplicate
- One staging model per source entity
- Materialized as `table` (full refresh is fine)
- Naming: `stg_<source>_<entity>.sql` (e.g., `stg_tmdb_movies.sql`)

**Marts (`models/marts/`):**
- Source: `staging.*` models only (never read raw directly)
- Implement star schema: `fact_*` tables with FK to `dim_*`
- Materialized as `table` or `incremental` depending on size
- Naming: `fact_<entity>.sql`, `dim_<entity>.sql`, `bridge_<entities>.sql`

**ML Features (`models/ml_features/`):**
- Source: `marts.*` models
- Aggregate or join for feature engineering
- Materialized as `table`

## YAML Descriptions Are Mandatory

Every model and every column **must** have a description in the YAML schema file.
These descriptions are used as context for the Step 10 text-to-SQL agent — vague descriptions produce bad SQL.

```yaml
models:
  - name: fact_movies
    description: >
      One row per movie. Contains all measurable attributes (budget, revenue,
      vote scores, runtime) with foreign keys to dimension tables.
    columns:
      - name: movie_id
        description: TMDB movie ID, primary key.
      - name: revenue
        description: Worldwide box office revenue in USD. Null if unreported.
```

## dbt Tests

Every model must have at minimum:
- `unique` + `not_null` on primary keys
- `relationships` for all foreign keys

## Iceberg Materialization Config

```sql
{{ config(
    materialized='table',
    properties={
        "format": "'PARQUET'",
        "partitioning": "ARRAY['year(release_date)']"
    }
) }}
```
